# Written BEFORE `git init`, deliberately. A video project's working directory
# is mostly media and rendered evidence; a single `git add -A` without this file
# commits gigabytes, and in the project this tool was extracted from it would
# also have committed unredacted licence plates and a device PIN.

# --- media, in and out -------------------------------------------------------
media/
source/
_cut/
_out/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mkv
*.webm
*.m4v
*.avi
*.wav
*.mp3
*.aac
*.flac

# Except the synthetic fixtures the tests generate/keep. They are tiny, carry no
# identity, and are produced by ffmpeg lavfi sources rather than filmed.
!tests/fixtures/**

# --- generated NLE / intermediate project files ------------------------------
# These embed absolute paths, and therefore the author's home directory.
*.kdenlive
*.mlt
*.edl
*.fcpxml
*.otio

# --- python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- agent / editor state ----------------------------------------------------
# Session state files carry usernames, transcript paths and cost telemetry.
.omc/
.claude/settings.local.json
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
